def get_weather():
    location = request.args.get('location')
    start_date = request.args.get('start_date')
    end_date = request.args.get('end_date')
    return WeatherForecast().get(location, start_date, end_date)

if __name__ == '__main__':
    app.run(debug=True)
```

This code establishes a Flask web application that integrates with multiple external APIs (primary and secondary weather services) to provide real-time weather forecasts and historical climate data for a specified geographical area. It utilizes a caching mechanism and a message queue system for efficient handling of concurrent requests, rate limiting, and high availability."]

